usage: diff_iso_usage [-h] [--min_expression MIN_EXPRESSION] [--log-stderr]
                      [--log-level LOG_LEVEL] [--log-conf LOG_CONF]
                      [--log-debug]
                      counts_matrix_tsv colname1 colname2 outfile

Calculates the usage of each isoform as a fraction of the total expression of
the gene and compares this between samples. It reads a flair quantify counts
matrix, or the counts of flair spliceevents (each alternative of an event) or
flair variantquant (the reads showing and not showing each allele).

positional arguments:
  counts_matrix_tsv     counts matrix TSV from flair quantify,
                        OUTPUT.spliceevents.counts.tsv from flair
                        spliceevents, or OUTPUT.var.counts.tsv from flair
                        variantquant
  colname1              the name of the column of the first sample
  colname2              the name of the column of the second sample
  outfile               output filename containing the p-value associated with
                        differential isoform usage for each isoform, and that
                        p-value adjusted for the isoforms tested (Benjamini-
                        Hochberg)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --min_expression MIN_EXPRESSION
                        an isoform with fewer than this many reads in the two
                        samples together is not tested, its p-values NA,
                        though its reads count toward its gene's other
                        isoforms. Filtering on the total, not on each sample,
                        leaves the adjusted p-values valid, and testing fewer
                        isoforms that could never be significant gives more
                        power (default: 0)
  --log-stderr          also log to stderr, even when logging to syslog
  --log-level LOG_LEVEL
                        Set level to integer or case-insensitive symbolic
                        value, one of: CRITICAL, FATAL, ERROR, WARN, WARNING,
                        INFO, DEBUG, NOTSET
  --log-conf LOG_CONF   Python logging configuration file, see
                        logging.config.fileConfig()
  --log-debug           short-cut that that sets --log-stderr and --log-
                        level=DEBUG
